Package: lindos-winapps
Version: 1.0.0
Section: otherosfs
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Lindos Team <team@lindos.dev>
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10), lindos-core (>= 1.0.0), freerdp3-x11 | freerdp2-x11
Recommends: lindos-vm | libvirt-daemon-system, desktop-file-utils
Suggests: podman
Homepage: https://lindos.dev
Description: Seamless Windows apps on Lindos over RDP (Adobe / Office)
 Runs individual Windows programs - Photoshop, Illustrator, Premiere, Word,
 Excel, PowerPoint, Outlook, File Explorer - each in its own window on the
 Lindos desktop, using FreeRDP RemoteApp against a backend Windows instance.
 This is the winapps-org/winapps pattern: the Windows program runs on real
 Windows (the lindos-vm libvirt VM "RDPWindows" by default, or an optional
 podman dockur/windows container) and only its window is forwarded over RDP.
 Ships:
  * lindos-winapps  — setup / check / list / install / run / remove.  'setup'
                      writes ~/.config/lindos/winapps/winapps.conf and points
                      you at FreeRDP credential handling; 'install <id>' puts a
                      Windows program in the Lindos menu; 'run <id>' launches it
                      through xfreerdp RemoteApp.
  * apps.json       — catalog of well-known Windows programs and their paths.
 Honesty: this needs a user-supplied, licensed Windows plus the licensed app
 installed inside the backend.  Lindos never downloads Windows, never enters or
 stores your Windows/app credentials, and never bypasses activation.  It is a
 real, honestly-labelled Windows session over RDP - not an emulator, and it
 does not defeat VM-blocking anti-cheat.
